intro	i1_explorer folders=33 file=viewer/scene.js · the owner's opening sentence (2026-11-13)	M: Developers can use Visual Studio Code to edit our source code.	M: Developers can use Visual Studio Code to edit our source code, where we enhanced it. | F: Enhanced how? | M: The editor now knows this project. Watch.
before	b2_f12_nothing builtin_defs=0 · b3_search_tests_only lines=9 files=2 all_in_tests=true	F: Where is the database set? | M: The editor cannot say.	F: Where is this database set? | M: Ask the editor. Go to definition... nothing. No definition found. | F: Then search for it? | M: Nine lines, all in two test files. None of them is the real one.
idea	§APP_SURFACE alias_only=1321 fields=1693	F: So how does anyone find it? | M: One object, two names. The project keeps its own index.	F: So how does anyone find it? | M: One object, two names. The code writes it under a short name, and reads it under a long one. More than thirteen hundred fields are written only under the short name. | M: So the project keeps its own index, made by its own script. The editor just reads it.
after	a1_hover written at viewer/city.js:717 · 14 writes · 704 reads · a2_jumped viewer/city.js line=717	F: And with the add-on? | M: Hover, and it tells you. Go to definition lands there.	F: And with the project's own add-on? | M: Hover. Written in the city file, line seven hundred seventeen. Fourteen writes, seven hundred and four reads. | F: And go to definition? | M: Now it lands on that line.
guess	p1_phantom PHANTOM · §APP_SURFACE phantom=282 · u1_unknown hover has no X0 text	F: What if nothing sets a field? | M: Then it says so. A phantom.	F: What if nothing ever sets a field? | M: Then it says so. Read, but never written: a phantom. There are two hundred and eighty-two of them. | F: And a field that does not exist? | M: It adds nothing. No answer beats a wrong answer.
tag	t1_tag spec places + printed by · t2_fake_tag no spec found	F: And these marks in the logs? | M: Each one is a rule. Hover for its page.	F: And these marks in the log lines? | M: Each one stands for a rule. Hover, and you get the pages that state it, and the line that prints it. | F: And a mark nobody wrote down? | M: It tells you plainly: no spec found.
fresh	e1_write_moved now_line=718 saved=true · e2 index stale · e3 written at viewer/city.js:718 seconds_after_first_ask	F: I just moved the code. | M: It refuses a wrong jump, then catches up.	F: Code moves. I just added a line above it, and saved. | M: Ask again. Index stale. It refuses to jump to the wrong line. | F: So now I fix it? | M: No. A few seconds later it has re-read the code. Line seven hundred eighteen.
stamp	l1_log_stamp line1 §LOG_STAMP commit= dirty=1 dirty_files=viewer/city.js	F: Can I trust an old log? | M: Read its first line.	F: Can I trust a log from yesterday? | M: Read its first line. It names the exact version of the code, and any file that was changed. Here, it names the file we just edited.
ship	r1_check §SHIP_CHECK verdict=PASS steps=3 · r2_cost status viewer: start-up · 234 KB · r3_lens lenses=1 §APP_SURFACE fields=1693	F: And before I ship? | M: Three more helpers, all first versions.	F: And before I ship a change? | M: Three more helpers, all first versions. A list in the side bar: run it, check it, and fetch it back from the live site. | F: What does my change cost? | M: It counts what every user downloads at start. This file: two hundred and thirty four kilobytes. | F: And that grey line? | M: The last value this line printed, from a saved log. Shown only when the log proves it came from this exact code.
limits	CODE_ARCHITECTURE_DESIGN §F.12 not-in-v1 lists · §X0_REALVSC vscode=1.146.0 · §F.10 only Linux was run	F: What can it not do yet? | M: It does not commit or deploy for you.	F: What can it not do yet? | M: It does not commit, or deploy, for you. It counts raw bytes, with no budget. And it has been proven on one version of the editor, on Linux.
close	§X0_ISOLATION deps=0 · §X0_MCP network_modules=0 · lib/ship.js fetchBack is the one network call · Developer Guide §4.1	M: No AI inside. No dependencies.	M: No AI inside. No dependencies. It uses the network only when you press fetch back. | M: Only what the project already knows, placed where you are working.
